Z||000000||jhar1987||04-08-2001||10:59 PM||||how can i convert 87-88 headlite motors to fit my 85? the 87-88 seem to be more reliable. thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Carrolles||04-09-2001||10:00 AM||||From what I've heard (at least I think so) you'll need the complete wiring harnes from the forward bulkhead (right near the power brake booster) forward to make it work.  Otherwise it is plug'n'play (with the later model motors of course).  Get one out of a donor car.<P>I bought one on e-bay for $5.00 US.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||04-09-2001||11:58 AM||||FWIW... I believe the Firebird motors will replace the Fiero motors. I think you have to swap 'em side-for-side. I believe the conversion to the new style motors occurred at about the same time in the Firebird. <BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
