Z||000005||StuGood||04-10-2001||10:46 AM||||Check out the Michigan Fiero Club's website.  Last I knew, it had a fairly complete description of how to do the conversion.  <P>You will need the electronic control box from the donor Fiero, which is located in the left front fender, ahead of the wheel well.<P>FWIW, on one of my cars, I modified the old-style headlight motors to work with the new-style controller.  I did this partly to avoid the cost of new motors, and partly just to see if it could be done.  In my opinion, it isn't worth doing.  Too much work, and the performance (response time) still isn't as good as with the new-style motors.<P>Get the new-style controller and new-style motors, take the time to do it right, and you should be happy with it.  Good luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
